{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>From where.</b> Like איה, and so אי הבל (Genesis 4:9), and the meaning of מזה is \"a place,\" as though he said: from where, a place, have you come?" "<b>Fleeing.</b> The resh is opened [spirantized] because of the guttural letter that follows it, and so בורַחַת כל העיר (Jeremiah 4:29), והיא כפורַחַת (Genesis 40:10), ברַחַת ובמזרה (Isaiah 30:24), and so יודַעַת איש (Numbers 31:17), because of the guttural letters that are after the rest of the [word]; and so the rule of the language is, no stranger is with us."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:46.847577329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}